Describe your solution (100 -200):
Appsibiti Prescription Reader Application (APRA), branded as AppsibitiRx, is an AI-Powered, full-stack web application that digitizes handwritten medical prescriptions using OpenAI's GPT-4o Vision
large language model.

The system targets pharmacists and healthcare providers in Nigeria, where the
overwhelming majority of prescriptions are still handwritten, creating significant risks of
misinterpretation, transcription errors, and lost records.

Pharmacists upload a photograph of a handwritten prescription. The system automatically extracts
structured data (drug names, dosages, frequencies, durations, and administration routes) from
the image and presents the results for human review. Pharmacists correct any errors before approval,
ensuring a human-in-the-loop safeguard.
The system combines Optical Character Recognition (OCR), Natural Language Processing (NLP), and pharmacist validation workflows to:

1. Improve readability of handwritten prescriptions;
2. Extract drug names, dosage instructions, frequency, route, and duration;
3. Identify ambiguous or incomplete prescriptions;
4. Support medication safety initiatives;
5. Reduce preventable dispensing errors;
6. Generate insights to improve prescribing practices.
